<title>UK: Courtaulds down after broker downgrade.</title>
<headline>Courtaulds down after broker downgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British chemicals group Courtaulds Plc fell on Thursday amid further reaction to yesterday's low-end profits and as Goldman Sachs cut the stock to &quot;market performer&quot; from &quot;market outperformer,&quot; traders said.</p>
<p>The stock was down 5p at 415 by 1152 GMT.</p>
<p>Analysts at Goldman were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
